an with no output.\n- **`pnpm --dir web lint`**: oxlint printed no problems. I read the empty output as clean and did not check its exit code separately.\n\nWhat changed, per file:\n\n- **`web/src/lib/rcq.ts`**: added `MAIN_SHARE = 0.02` and `splitOptions()`. `expectedOptions()` now collects every label per key. A key with one label is named by it, and a key with several is named by the key. Its share is the sum of its rows at the chosen tier. Tier choice, `decks` totals and sorting are unchanged, and the doc comment is updated.\n- **`web/src/components/rcq/InputsCard.tsx`**: a `showOther` flag (default false) splits the chips into main, the shown or picked `other` options, then the kept `missing` ones. When some `other` options are hidden, an `Other (N)` button appears, and it switches to `Fewer` when expanded. It has `aria-expanded` and the same 44px pill style as the chips.\n- **`web/src/views/RcqView.tsx`**: dropped `useMetagameStatus` and the reset-based window. Presence now reads `{ days: CHIP_WINDOW_DAYS }` with `CHIP_WINDOW_DAYS = 14`. The share note uses the wording from the spec.\n\nChoices I made that the spec left open:\n- A key's labels are collected across all tiers, not just the chosen one, so the \"several labels\" decision doesn't change with the tier.\n- The `Other` button also shows `Fewer` when expanded even if no options are hidden, so a user can collapse it.\n\nNothing is committed. The worktree has these three modified files plus the untracked `SPEC.md`, which was already there.", "ttft_ms": 2179, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 41598, "uuid": "8f040051-188f-4625-9bbc-0427756944e1", "ttft_stream_ms": 2091, "time_to_request_ms": 342, "first_content_frame_ms": 2092, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
